{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner adopts the builder's text-first direction for generic thread names, with a precise fallback. A thread's nonempty goal still comes first. For its opening declared act, titleOf prefers the first present body field by name whose field type in that act's D(s) is text, excluding scope and because. If no such field is present, keep the current first-present-field value fallback and formatting. When the opening act is unavailable, keep the thread-ID fallback. Legacy, platform, unknown and label-only uses without declared field metadata retain their existing behavior. This lets Start a song choose its declared title text over the earlier-named key enum while keeping nontext-only acts informative.\n\nText means the declared/step field type, rather than JavaScript typeof string: enum keys, member/act IDs and SHA values are strings too. Use the opening record's own declaration and applicable step fields under D(s), never the currently active declaration. Sort by name so typed bodies and canonical recorded bodies give the same title. The shared pure helper remains the owner for client, CLI, MCP and UI; no new declaration member or binding change is introduced. If target metadata is needed for a step-owned field, carry it explicitly through the shared helper and callers while retaining the existing public fallback. Keep the evaluator out of the reader import.\n\nUpdate the helper/type documentation, section33.10 and open point52, all affected reader expectations and READMEs together. Retain the browser's Footprints and So What assertions and run the entire case through its form validation, acceptance and final lane checks. Add meaningful paired vectors with identical string values in enum/text fields, different body insertion/canonical orders, absent optional text, no text field, legacy/unknown fallbacks and relabelled historical D(s). New guards require compiling named semantic failures as part of the original complete review.\n\nThe current title 'Start a song: c' follows the previous explicit first-field-by-name rule; the browser expectation is from an earlier rule. This is a deliberate reader-design change. My earlier 7fd wording should not be read as proof that Footprints already followed that adopted rule. The two unavailable-read UI publication failures in0fd98c41 remain separately owed. All five stage-5 conditions, full surfaces/legacy/grants, final composed gates/review and existing platform owners remain intact; this decision adds no first-Jam readiness condition.","body":{"decision":"Adopt text-first naming for declared acts, with the existing fallback retained.","scope":"Planner decision for section 33.10/open point52 within the full stage-5 request.","source_head":"5590c318b9210bfee08756f747d7893b58bf1ea4","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}